Both Alice and Bob are correct in their statements. 

- Alice correctly states that water freezes at 0 degrees Celsius. At -10 degrees Celsius, water is below freezing, so it remains liquid.
- Bob correctly acknowledges that water does not freeze at -10 degrees Celsius, but he also correctly notes that he is right. This implies that his statement is accurate, and he is not wrong.

Therefore, both are right. [end of text]


